& [FSC2FinalSlicesExplosion] is the processing pass that mints final work slices inside FSC2 planning coordination
  + [root_subject] is FSC2 planning coordination
  + [chunk_state] is activated_by_FSC1_foundation_contract_pack
  + [boundary_input] is FSC1 foundation contract pack
  + [unresolved_external_dependency_set] is empty_after_gate
  + [slice_strategy] is order slices so imported boundary contracts are mapped before operator refinement, then packetization, coordination, completion gates, fixtures, and final pack acceptance
  + [result] is seven final slices, one ready now and six gated inside FSC2

  = must: preserve no unresolved dependency outside FSC2
  = must: make each slice contiguous by expected output and verification oracle
  = must: run completed-work review after each completed slice
  = must: mark downstream slices stale when an upstream accepted output changes

## Fold 1: Boundary And Imported Contracts

& [Fold1BoundaryAndImportedContracts] is the boundary check for FSC2 final slices
  + [inside_boundary] is P4 whole-field planning and packetization, P7 coordination and multi-agent governance, and P8b readiness, packetization, completion-review, and coordination fixtures
  + [accepted_boundary_input] is docs/planning/FSC1_Foundation_Contract_Pack.v1.sop
  + [forbidden_external_dependency] is FSC3 runtime graph proof, FSC4 surface projection, FSC5 operations safety, live machine control, production dispatch, and unreviewed schema mutation

  = must: import FSC1 records, operator template, foundation operator contracts, storage decision, and foundation fixtures as accepted boundary inputs
  = must: refine readiness and packetization inside FSC2 rather than editing FSC1
  = must: keep runtime graph and surface projection outside FSC2

## Fold 2: Slice Chain

& [Fold2SliceChain] is the ordered final slice chain
  + [FSC2-S01] is imported boundary and invariant map
  + [FSC2-S02] is planning readiness operator contract
  + [FSC2-S03] is work packet generation contract
  + [FSC2-S04] is coordination claim and rendezvous contracts
  + [FSC2-S05] is completion review delta gate contract
  + [FSC2-S06] is planning coordination fixture plan
  + [FSC2-S07] is FSC2 completion review and activation packet

  = must: keep FSC2-S01 as the only ready slice at first minting
  = must: activate later slices only when their inside-FSC2 inputs are accepted

## Fold 3: Model Routing

& [Fold3ModelRouting] is the route classification for FSC2 slices
  + [FSC2-S01] is requires deeper reasoning
  + [FSC2-S02] is requires deeper reasoning
  + [FSC2-S03] is requires deeper reasoning
  + [FSC2-S04] is requires deeper reasoning
  + [FSC2-S05] is requires deeper reasoning
  + [FSC2-S06] is GPT-5.3-Codex-Spark-suitable after FSC2-S01 through FSC2-S05 are accepted
  + [FSC2-S07] is requires deeper reasoning

  = must: state model route on every slice
  = must: keep readiness semantics, packet boundaries, coordination authority, and completion gate behavior under deeper reasoning
  = should: route fixture drafting to GPT-5.3-Codex-Spark only after contracts stabilize

## Fold 4: Readiness And Gates

& [Fold4ReadinessAndGates] is the current FSC2 readiness pass
  + [ready_slice] is FSC2-S01
  + [gated_slice] is FSC2-S02 until FSC2-S01 accepted
  + [gated_slice] is FSC2-S03 until FSC2-S02 accepted
  + [gated_slice] is FSC2-S04 until FSC2-S03 accepted
  + [gated_slice] is FSC2-S05 until FSC2-S02, FSC2-S03, and FSC2-S04 accepted
  + [gated_slice] is FSC2-S06 until FSC2-S05 accepted
  + [gated_slice] is FSC2-S07 until FSC2-S06 accepted

  = must: not start a gated slice until its activation gate is accepted
  = must: run completion review before opening the next slice

& [FSC2FinalSlicesConclusion] is the result of this pass
  + [ready_for] is execution of FSC2-S01 imported boundary and invariant map
  + [not_ready_for] is FSC3 runtime graph implementation, surface implementation, operations safety work, or production dispatch
  + [remaining_uncertainty] is readiness semantics, packet boundary semantics, coordination claim conflict handling, and completion-review delta behavior

  = must: promote the final slice surface only with satisfaction signature and source lineage
